      clinicalImportance: 'Hemodialysis is essential for patients with end-stage renal disease (ESRD) or acute kidney injury. It removes urea, creatinine, potassium, and excess water that would otherwise accumulate to toxic levels. Without dialysis, uremia, hyperkalemia, and fluid overload would be fatal within days to weeks.',
