      history: 'BiPAP was developed in the late 1980s by Respironics (now Philips) as an evolution of CPAP to provide pressure support ventilation. The bilevel approach was found to improve ventilation and CO2 clearance in hypercapnic patients. Modern BiPAP devices include backup rate, AVAPS (average volume assured pressure support), and advanced trigger/cycle algorithms.',
